      "task": "Express six positions in one arithmetic progression using a_1 and d, including symbolic and doubled indices.",
      "solution": "There are r-1 increments from a_1 to a_r. Hence a_3=a_1+2d; a_26=a_1+25d; a_260=a_1+259d; a_m=a_1+(m-1)d; a_(m+1)=a_1+md; a_(2m)=a_1+(2m-1)d. m is a positive integer.",
      "distinction": "The index is not the number of increments; doubling an index is not doubling a term."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "233",
