      "task": "Solve all four systems for the first term and d; enumerate every real solution when nonlinear conditions allow more than one.",
      "solution": "First: a_10-a_3=7d=21, so d=3; a_1+a_7=2a_1+6d=42, so a_1=12. Second: 2a_1+14d=-0.2 and 2a_1+12d=2.6; subtracting gives 2d=-2.8, so d=-1.4 and a_1=9.7. Third: a_1+a_5=2a_3=24 fixes a_3=12. The product a_2*a_3=60 fixes a_2=5, so d=7 and a_1=-2. This system has one solution, despite its product. Fourth: a_2+a_3+a_4=3a_3=3 gives a_3=1. Then a_2*a_4=(1-d)(1+d)=1-d^2=-8, so d^2=9, d=3 or -3. The complete solution pairs are (a_1,d)=(-5,3) and (7,-3). They give triples (-2,1,4) and (4,1,-2), respectively, both with sum 3 and product of the outside terms -8.",
